Chapter: VecExtractHazards
  cites Foreword chapter Console

 Regression probes for two emitter hazards in the extract builtins,
 both found during the VecArray stage and fixed together. First, a
 call in receiver position returns its cell pointer raw in RAX; the
 index operand's temp allocation could land on RAX when the rotation
 wrapped, zeroing the receiver before the load - the extract then
 read address zero, which demand paging happily serves as zeros.
 Second, the emitters shifted the index register in place; when the
 index was a register-resident local, the variable itself was
 corrupted for every later read. Each probe below computes a wrong
 value if its hazard returns. The chain of bindings before the
 call-receiver extracts varies the temp-rotation position so the
 old collision is exercised at multiple offsets.

Section: Makers

  make-vec : Real -> Vector 2 Real
  make-vec (x) = vec-splat x

  make-vec4 : Integer -> Vector 4 (Real approximate)
  make-vec4 (seed) = vec4-splat (to-real-approx (real-from-int seed))

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console] Nothing
  opening = act
    let a = 100
    in let b = a + 1
    in let c = b + 1
    in let d = c + 1
    in let e = d + 1
    in let f = e + 1
    in let g = f + 1
    in let x0 = vec-extract (make-vec 7.5) 0
    in let x1 = vec-extract (make-vec 8.5) 1
    in let x2 = vec-extract (make-vec 9.5) 0
    in let x3 = vec-extract (make-vec 10.5) 1
    in let x4 = vec-extract (make-vec 11.5) 0
    in let x5 = vec-extract (make-vec 12.5) 1
    in let idx = 1
    in let v = make-vec 42.0
    in let picked = vec-extract v idx
    in let idx-after = idx + 10
    in let q = make-vec4 9
    in let q1 = vec4-extract q idx
    in let idx-final = idx + 100
    in act
      print-line-uni ("x0: " & show x0)
      print-line-uni ("x1: " & show x1)
      print-line-uni ("x2: " & show x2)
      print-line-uni ("x3: " & show x3)
      print-line-uni ("x4: " & show x4)
      print-line-uni ("x5: " & show x5)
      print-line-uni ("picked: " & show picked)
      print-line-uni ("idx-after: " & show idx-after)
      print-line-uni ("idx-final: " & show idx-final)
      print-line-uni ("chain: " & show g)
    end
  end
